{"title":"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At the start of the day a vending machine had 42 sandwiches in it:\n</p>\n<ul><li>13 chicken sandwiches at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/6/6565e6f9e1251a34c91347988e7ccc3f04880649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 each * 14 cheese sandwiches at$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"245\" height=\"14\" />3 each</li>\n<li>15 egg sandwiches at <span style=\"color:red\">$2.50 each</span></li></ul>\n<p>At the end of the day the total money made was$ (Error compiling LaTeX. Unknown error_msg)61, of which <span style=\"color:red\">$21 came from cheese sandwich sales. What additional piece of information would allow us to solve the question &quot;How many sandwiches of each type were left at the end of the day?&quot;\n</span></p><p>(A) Total price of remaining sandwiches.\n(B) Number of remaining sandwiches.\n(C) Total price of sandwiches at the beginning of the day.\n(D) Number of remaining cheese sandwiches.\n(E) No additional information is needed.\n</p><p>== Solution ==\nFrom$ (Error compiling LaTeX. Unknown error_msg)21 in cheese sales, exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c127dcd344ac6ed1e1e225da4da8a49cf78f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 \\div 3 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> cheese sandwiches were sold, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341d8abeb71c594dd67d716c98c0e851b6669e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - 7 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> cheese sandwiches. \n</p><p>The remaining revenue from chicken (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) and egg (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) sandwiches is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e52e97c220f7be81719245eacbaecc1c8a8853e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61 - 21 = \\$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />:\n</p>\n<dl><dd><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37159241cc8631462758ba3948c9e6cbbd640e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3C + 2.5E = 40 \\implies 6C = 80 - 5E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"289\" height=\"16\" /></dd></dl>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/4/de4eb848fdad587316a093317bef9c45222b01d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> must be a multiple of 5 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f031edf0161f6871c0423eccfad50c1ab06c811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C \\le 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can be 0, 5, or 10.\n</p>\n<ul><li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85aac914361efb48aaa13187304c1c5bdfef0589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 0$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5a165a691650ce20bbe42d697cd960f42f8430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> (impossible since we started with 15 egg sandwiches).</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/deff46f14c0d78c3bc8849130d19227b6a72aa34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57315a37d0cd67ffd503bf185114046c7c3fcad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, leaving 8 chicken, 7 cheese, and 5 egg sandwiches (total 20 remaining).</li>\n<li>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/a/05ae1f77c2b2572405eadbce494ce9ccab5ae38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/4/61466ea67ef9dd63312dc77d5c5569aa51968b8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, leaving 3 chicken, 7 cheese, and 11 egg sandwiches (total 21 remaining).</li></ul>\n<p>Since there are two valid scenarios, knowing the total number of remaining sandwiches distinguishes between them.\n</p><p><b>Answer:</b> <b>(B)</b>~prince_penguin_V\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problem/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problem/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">2021 CJMC Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Canada_Jay_Mathematical_Competition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Canada Jay Mathematical Competition\">Canada Jay Mathematical Competition</a></li></ul>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CJMC_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 CJMC Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018014731\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 95/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3483/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:38019:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018014731 and revision id 293567. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}